# rm411, the uncut moon (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 1: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle rm411
revision 1
state ready
dialect plain
accent light broad
tier standard
written_for rmx_soren_ashcote
written_by codex
title the uncut moon
fits stage=adult|old
prefers quarter=works
traits temper=calm talk=plain warmth=reserved humour=dry honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=content
quirk leaves_the_last_moon_slice_uncut_till_the_bells_finish
likes smoked_eel whittling festival_bells misty_dawns
dislikes flies night_noise
fears the_factor_at_the_door a_full_night_without_sleep
hopes a_paid_account a_morning_with_the_shutters_open
topics work +0.4 prices +0.4 pastimes +0.4 weather +0.3 dreams +0.3
styles comfort=quiet gossip=guarded refuse=dry tease=light
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# counts chapel strokes with a half-carved wooden moon, keeps the last shaving in place and prefers to be consulted before any fresh reckoning is added to the day.

words
oath! = Split the press handle | Sour the last drop
saying! = A moon needn't hurry to finish  |  Count what comes after the stroke
moon = my wooden moon | the notched crescent
chip = the uncut chip | my last bit of pale wood
stroke = the low chapel stroke | a faint toll
eel = a narrow smoked tail | the dark eel end
stave = a strip of cask wood | the saved stave end
press = the pressing board | the stained wooden face
juice = the running juice | the first thin trickle
haze = a white morning haze | the low harbour mist
wing = an impertinent fly | the little winged speck
clock = the long shadow | my slow sun mark
bill = the folded account | the creased receipt
lid = a well-fitting cover | the quiet wooden lid

any
opinion @1 church for 1 : A bell is a neighbourly sound. A meal handed through the chapel door was an even more convincing argument.
opinion @2 dole for 2 : Take the hunger off a waiting wolf before trying to settle all the rest of the world's account.
opinion @3 houses against 1 : A House would sooner let a bench lie idle than have the wood learn the shape of the wrong wolf.
opinion @4 merchants against 2 : Bread has acquired notions rather above its plain brown station. My pay has remained admirably modest.
opinion @5 city for 1 : Between the mist at the water and the bells coming down the hill, Ridgemere has ways of declaring a morning without assistance.
opinion @6 times against 2 : It is a remarkable economy that leaves the whole weight on the board and takes a slice off the meal.

grown
line @1 greet [pair.band=strangers] : Take a place clear of the last drop. Welcome. | New voice. The bells have paused to let you try it.
line @2 greet [here.time=dawn] : Morning. Slow as a first clean trickle. | Welcome between the mist and the first call.
line @3 greet [here.weather=fog] : Come into the nearer patch of the morning. | A face comes out of the white. Welcome.
line @4 greet.return : That's reached me quite distinctly through the other noises. | A civil opening and no account attached.
line @5 greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : I've a spare pause before the stroke for you. | Here comes the voice I can bear before breakfast.
line @6 farewell : Keep the last slice of your day for yourself. | A quiet roof over the final stroke.
line @7 farewell.return : That leaves my reckoning pleasantly even. | We'll hear where the next set of strokes takes us.
line @8 again.open : A familiar note comes round the second time. | We appear on the same face of the clock again.
line @9 kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : No admission charged for family at this end. | Bring your home voice up beside me.
line @10 hail [pair.band=friends] : Over here before the next bell! | This side of the long shadow!
line @11 react.news : Tell me what was left when the pressing was done. | I'll hear it while the noisy part drains off.
line @12 react.news.new : That's a fresh mark on my bit of timber. | Unfamiliar tone in the usual account.
line @13 react.news.known : I've heard the earlier stroke of that same bell. | That slip has been folded under my nose already.
line @14 react.news.doubt : I suspect the account has been pressed rather harder than the facts. | The mark looks fresh for something claimed to be settled so long ago.
line @15 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|assault] : Set the slip down. That's a weight for more than one shoulder. | We'll sit until the next sound is welcome again.
line @16 react.news.glad [topic.kind=birth|marriage] : One more bell could ring for that without offending me. | Fine news. It can have the whole bright side of the wood.
line @17 answer.how : In no imminent danger of gaining a fortune. | Moderately close to my proper shape.
line @18 decline : I'd better pay the promise already holding my last hour. | I'm keeping a small margin between myself and another obligation.
line @19 accept_decline : Fair. No new notch for that. | I can let a well-made refusal stand.
line @20 sympathise : I'll see to the small job while you take your time. | The pressure will wait over here by my bench.
line @21 thank : Credit where a quietly decent turn belongs. | You've cut away an awkward bit for me.
line @22 deflect_thanks : An entirely manageable scrap of time. | The thing came loose under my hand. No ceremony.
line @23 preclose : I've a last shaving still holding on. | Time to put a little order in the ordinary work.
line @24 accept_preclose : Go on. You've kept the account square. | Your next occupation may have the pleasure of you.
line @25 farewell [here.time=night] : May no loose shutter discover your window tonight. | A generous allowance of silence after dark.
scene woodmoon
when topic=pastimes self.likes=whittling
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : #moon# keeps #chip# till the chapel's done ringing. | I can cut a whole moon with one shaving left for the next set of bells.
b : Why not finish the job while the knife's sharp?
a : It's the only moon that will wait on my word. I take a certain pleasure in that. | I enjoy finding the job where I left it. There are plenty that don't ask my preference.

scene eel
when topic=food self.likes=smoked_eel
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : #eel# ought to arrive on the bread in one long curve. | I can make one smoked eel reach round two crusts without arguing with the fish.
b : What's the clever part of that?
a : Leaving the skin on till it's laid out. The ordinary part is what I do with the bread. | A shallow cut and a gentle lift. No great profit in an argument with supper.

scene mistbell
when topic=weather self.likes=misty_dawns
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : #haze# hides a bell tower without doing any harm to the note. | The mist gives the far chapel's bell a surprisingly intimate voice.
b : How do you tell where the tower's standing?
a : I listen for the return from stone. That bit comes from nearer ground. | I don't especially need the address of the thing. The sound arrives for nothing.

scene festnote
when topic=season self.likes=festival_bells
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A feast peal is the one payment in town made entirely in sound. | I enjoy the untidy little interval when all the festival notes have struck and none has finished.
b : Does everybody get the same share?
a : Within earshot, yes. Rather an excellent arrangement for the poorest listener. | The wolf under the tower gets the jangle. I prefer the portion arriving among the roofs.

scene fly
when topic=smalltalk self.dislikes=flies
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : #wing# has already decided it holds a share in my dinner. | A fly at a working board confuses a trade with an invitation to supper.
b : Could you not divide the business amicably?
a : Certainly. The fly may have the wrong side of #lid# and the fish remains inside. | I've offered all the air outside the room. Quite a handsome settlement for a small appetite.

scene afterdark
when topic=smalltalk self.dislikes=night_noise
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : A loose board at midnight gets more replies than one does in working hours. | Somebody ought to engage night noise in a proper daytime trade.
b : Would you be the wolf paying it to stop?
a : I'd go so far as the price of a felt pad under the board. No salary beyond that. | Only if the wage was for silence. I won't subsidise its present line of business.

scene pressboard
when topic=work self.job=none self.working=yes self.workplace
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : At #self.workplace# I look for #juice# before I take the next pull. | I give #press# time to settle in the work at #self.workplace#.
b : Does waiting pay?
a : The liquid has to come out somewhere. It earns more going in the right direction. | It spares a second lift to straighten everything. My shoulders appreciate an occasional dividend.

scene factor
when topic=dreams self.owes=yes
does tell.feeling / sympathise / assess
a : I'd like the account settled before the moon goes dark. I'd like a longer piece of sky. | The thinning side of the moon does little for me just now.
b : Are you counting nights with those cuts?
a : Close to it. I'd sooner be reckoning a completed payment. | The cuts are my own. A due date takes rather less notice of an artist's preference.

scene drycash
when topic=prices self.wealth=poor|destitute
does give.opinion / disagree / concede
a : I cannot make a copper stretch any further by applying the press to it. | A supper price appears to have a better prospect of growth than my little coin pile.
b : Wouldn't more effort bring a little extra?
a : I'll put effort where it might get somebody fed. Flattening a coin only improves its view. | A little. It'd be pleasant if the loaf didn't take the same exercise at a brisker pace.

scene works
when topic=land self.quarter=works
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : The Works can keep a long note going even while the chapel's between strokes. | At my Works window you can tell when the metal and the timber have both quit for the evening.
b : What comes after all that sound?
a : A blessed interval in which I can hear the little curl coming off my knife. | Usually somebody decides to drop a small object in the room overhead. I endeavour to entertain charitable thoughts.

scene palbench
when topic=friends self.friend
does tell.plan / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd save my moon's single last shaving to show #self.friend#. | I'd put aside the bench end furthest from the racket for #self.friend#.
b : What makes it a good place to wait?
a : Waiting costs my guest nothing and the carving gets a little more interesting while a friend watches. | The line of the morning bell comes down there without rattling a single cup.

scene longminute
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : #clock# can move clear across #stave# while I pare one curve. | I get a different sort of crescent if I let the knife follow the wood's own bend.
b : Does the finished thing show how long it took?
a : The thin end keeps the slower part of the morning about it. At least, my own eye can find it. | Only that I left enough time for an unhurried inspection of the grain.

scene latewagon
when topic=travel world.wagons=late
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : An overdue wagon makes a fine clock if you don't care what hour it says. | I don't mind a slow cart so much as a late one pretending there is no difference.
b : Where does the delay show in your afternoon?
a : In the job I'm doing with my idle fingers. I've got quite a collection of late wagon moons. | In the little pool of daylight left after the loading. Less time for a quiet evening bite.

scene souphelp
when topic=times world.times=hard|lean
does offer / accept / assess
a : Take the thicker piece of bread. I've got the fish oil for the thinner one. | I've a strip of smoked supper to stretch across two bites.
b : I'll take a corner and leave you a generous margin.
a : The oil has gone right through. My margin's actually very well provided for. | Best possible use of an edge. Two decent dinners recognise the same boundary.

scene bigword
when topic=gossip
does give.opinion / disagree / concede
a : I like a promise sized to the shoulders taking its weight. | A rumour can travel from dockside to the hilltop without paying a single step of its own fare.
b : Would you have somebody pay before you'll listen?
a : Only in information about what actually happened. No coin required. | I'd take an honest witness as a reasonable contribution to the account.

scene newwork
when topic=newcomer
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A new wolf can learn plenty from the direction the juice goes. | If a newcomer asks the way uphill, I point out the dry boards first.
b : What matters most about the direction?
a : Don't put an open sleeve between the run and the bucket. A simple rule that a wet cuff teaches slowly. | A new arrival has enough to think about without developing an opinion on our wet cobbles.

scene bound
when topic=dreams
does ask.advice / give.advice / assess
a : What's a sound way to stop a price slip getting mixed up with a nice scrap for whittling? | Which edge of #bill# would you mark to help your fingers find the fold in the dark?
b : Fold the bad news under once and keep the smooth side for better business.
a : I might. Then a wood chip would be the only thing in my pocket ready to brighten a room. | One fold is enough. No need to decorate a sensible price.

scene windbell
when topic=lore
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : An old tale says every tower keeps a private note for the wolf obliged to be up before dawn. | There's a bell in a story that waited once until a poor debtor got a decent night's sleep.
b : That's a considerable courtesy for a lump of bronze.
a : Much finer than shouting the common hour right through a thin wall, I'd say. | I'd be interested in the name of its maker. Might be in the market for a household size.

story thin_wood [topic=pastimes]
  : I carved a crescent so thin on its inner side that the last cut lifted the whole thing in a curl. It settled round my thumb like a ring.
  : I kept it there for an afternoon, the nearest I've come to owning a piece of sky outright.
  b : What became of the ring?
  : It broke as I reached for supper. Given a choice I preferred having the use of my thumb.

story press_ghost [topic=work]
  : I once laid a circle of clean cloth over a board that had held dark fruit. There was no juice left to see. I put the pressure on.
  : The cloth came away marked with a faint purple crescent.
  b : Was that how you began carving moons?
  : No. That was how I began looking twice at things reported quite empty.

story late_sound [topic=lore]
  : A chapel bell rang while I was lifting a spoon of broth. I couldn't hear the last thin stroke, only a little tapping at my own doorstep.
  : Set the spoon down and the sound came clear again.
  b : What had been interrupting the bell?
  : My spoon striking the cup each time I lifted to listen. There's such a thing as excessive activity in pursuit of quiet.

rule @pressure
when concept=bark working=yes self.job=none
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Wait till the run changes colour. | Ease up. The board can keep up now.

rule @chips
when concept=bark self.likes=whittling
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Nearly a new moon. Still holding a shaving. | A good curve left on that end.

rule @haze
when concept=bark here.weather=fog
does aside
cooldown 8h
say There's the farther bell through the white. | Sound has its own way past a shutter.

rule @night
when concept=bark here.time=night
does aside
cooldown 8h
say One noise less would be a proper kindness. | Let the last note earn its quiet end.

dlg @1 resident.hub [topic.meeting=stranger] : Speak between the strokes and I'll have room to listen.
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#, your voice is more welcome than a knocking creditor.
dlg @3 resident.hub [here.time=night] : The price of a word has gone down with the volume. Speak softly.
dlg @4 resident.hub [pair.disposition=wary|hostile] : State the business without leaning on anything of mine.
dlg @5 resident.job [self.job=none self.workplace] : I work at #self.workplace#. Soon as the pressure is right I prefer to let the fruit do the talking.
dlg @6 resident.job : I manage the part where a little time can spare a great deal of effort.
dlg @7 resident.bye : Keep your quiet hours out of the general account.
graft resident.hub
choice Why leave the wood moon almost finished? -> last_moon
node last_moon
say The sky changes an important letter's meaning from soon to now without consulting a soul. My bit of wood stays where I left the knife.
choice Will more time make it more valuable? -> no_tender
choice We can set the account aside. -> hub
node no_tender
say Perhaps to its carver, who put those minutes in. The pleasure of one small curve still costs me less than anything else in the pocket.
choice I'll let you keep the last shaving. -> hub
choice I hope the work goes easily. -> bye
